   "reason": "DATA_GAP:capex \u2014 capex missing for FY2023, FY2024, FY2025 (and every other year) in EDGAR companyfacts under every candidate tag the engine reads, because APA files its capital expenditures only as additions to oil and gas property under PaymentsToExploreAndDevelopOilAndGasProperties (the only capex-like Payments* tag in its companyfacts). The engine applies this single value to every missing period; $2,740M is both the FY2025 filed figure and the median of the three filed years ($2,313M / $2,851M / $2,740M). Against the true per-year figures it overstates FY2023 capex by $427M (conservative direction, lowers that year's OE) and understates FY2024 by $111M (~3% of that year's filed OCF, raising that year's OE slightly \u2014 noted, not hidden); FY2025 is exact. The median-of-3 base year is FY2024 on shares, and the single-value fill lands the computed median base within ~1% of the median built from the true per-year figures, so the approximation does not drive the verdict. A separate small line, leasehold and property acquisitions ($26M in FY2025), is acquisition spend, not additions to oil and gas property, and is excluded as the filer presents it.",
